    "rich_text_czWEgw": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_kYqBzH": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Gemstone Buying Guide: How to Choose the Right Gemstone",
            "use_h1": true
          }
        },
        "text_jUByfz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Gemstone jewelry offers a distinct combination of color, individuality, and craftsmanship. From classic sapphires and emeralds to modern birthstone pieces, choosing the right gemstone requires an understanding of quality, origin, and durability.</p><p>At Milano Jewelry, we work with both precious and semi-precious gemstones, carefully selected for color, clarity, and overall composition—so you can choose with confidence.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "subheading_JXaHAf": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What Are Gemstones?"
          }
        },
        "text_hNnGUx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Gemstones are naturally occurring minerals or organic materials that are cut and polished for use in jewelry. Their value is determined by factors such as color, clarity, rarity, and durability.</p><p>Gemstones are broadly categorized into:</p><ul><li><strong>Precious gemstones</strong> (such as diamond, ruby, sapphire, emerald)<br/></li><li><strong>Semi-precious gemstones</strong> (such as amethyst, topaz, citrine, garnet)<br/></li></ul><p>Both categories offer unique beauty and are widely used across fine jewelry.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_kYqBzH",
        "text_jUByfz",
        "subheading_JXaHAf",
        "text_hNnGUx"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".subheading {color: #002058; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 6px;}"
      ],
      "name": "Rich text",
      "settings": {
        "height": "small",
