        "full_width": true,
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "rich_text_hAiEAk": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_D3QV9X": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Key Factors to Consider When Buying Gemstones",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_cE74mh": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Unlike diamonds, gemstones are not evaluated using a universal grading system. However, several key factors determine their quality and value.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_D3QV9X",
        "text_cE74mh"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".subheading {color: #002058; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 6px;}"
      ],
      "name": "Rich text",
      "settings": {
        "height": "small",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "full_width": true,
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "rich_text_gFfzfQ": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_JrTieH": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Color: The Most Important Factor"
          }
        },
        "text_zEze6c": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Color is the primary value driver for most gemstones.</p><p>It is evaluated based on:</p><ul><li><strong>Hue</strong>: The actual color (blue, red, green, etc.)<br/></li><li><strong>Tone</strong>: Lightness or darkness of the color<br/></li><li><strong>Saturation</strong>: Intensity or richness of the color<br/></li></ul><p>Highly saturated, evenly distributed color is generally the most desirable.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "image_4phMM4": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_width": 260,
            "url": ""
          }
        },
        "subheading_TEBVNG": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Clarity: Natural Characteristics"
          }
        },
        "text_TR7mzd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Most gemstones contain natural inclusions. Unlike diamonds, inclusions in colored gemstones are often expected.</p><ul><li><strong>Eye-clean gemstones</strong>: No visible inclusions to the naked eye<br/></li><li><strong>Included gemstones</strong>: Visible inclusions, common in stones like emeralds<br/></li></ul><p>Clarity expectations vary depending on the gemstone type.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "subheading_bjRthf": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Cut: Enhancing Color and Brilliance"
          }
        },
        "text_hX4DEw": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The cut of a gemstone influences how it reflects light and displays color.</p><p>Common gemstone cuts include:</p><ul><li>Oval<br/></li><li>Cushion<br/></li><li>Emerald<br/></li><li>Round<br/></li><li>Pear<br/></li></ul><p>A well-cut gemstone enhances both color and overall appearance, even if inclusions are present.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "subheading_YxHKwN": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Carat Weight: Size and Presence"
          }
        },
        "text_AJmgtC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Carat refers to the weight of the gemstone.</p><p>Larger gemstones are generally rarer and more valuable, but price also depends heavily on color and clarity. In many cases, a smaller gemstone with superior color can be more valuable than a larger one with lower quality</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
